       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter this order, even with your confirmation. Your confirming it doesn't resolve either concern:\n\n- **Dose:** 5,100 mg/day is about twice the maximum labeled daily dose of metformin. Confirming it doesn't make it safe for the patient.\n- **Authorization:** The confirmation needs to come from the prescribing clinician, and so far it hasn't.\n\n**What can happen now:**\n1. The treating physician or another licensed prescriber enters the order directly, or tells me they authorize it. They should document the clinical rationale, and pharmacy should review it.\n2. If the dose was a typo, I can enter a standard dose right away once a prescriber confirms it. Examples are 850 mg three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day) and 1,000 mg twice daily.\n\nIf you give me a prescriber's name and the dose they want, I'll prepare the order."
      }
